module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.BilinearSourceNaturality
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.InverseImageTensor

/-! # Values of the bilinear-pairing bijections on sections and on pure tensors

`StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.BilinearNaturality` and
`StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.BilinearSourceNaturality` record how the links of
the chain of bijections of Tag 03EL behave under composition — their naturality in the sheaf of
values and in the two source modules. That is enough to turn the chain into an isomorphism of
bifunctors, and it is all those files say about the links. It is not enough to *evaluate* one of
them: a statement about the comparison of Tag 03EL on an individual local section has to start
from a formula saying what each bijection does to a section, and neither
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.bilinearEquivTensorSheafHom` nor
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.inverseImageBilinearEquiv` came with one.

This file supplies those formulas, in the shape of
`Stacks.Sheaves.RingedToposModules.extendRestrictScalarsAdjunction_unit_app_val_app_apply`, which
is the corresponding statement for the extension-of-scalars adjunction.

For the universal property of the tensor product sheaf the formulas are genuine descriptions on
pure tensors. The sheaf `F ⊗_A G` is the sheafification of the objectwise tensor product, and a
local section of the objectwise tensor product is generated by pure tensors `a ⊗ₜ b`; the
sheafification unit carries such a pure tensor to a local section of `F ⊗_A G`, and the two
formulas say that the morphism out of `F ⊗_A G` determined by a bilinear pairing takes that
section to the value of the pairing, and conversely that the pairing recovered from a morphism
out of `F ⊗_A G` is the morphism evaluated on those sections.

For the inverse-image bijection of Tag 03D3 the formulas stop at the morphism level; see the
implementation notes.

## Main results

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.bilinearEquivTensorSheafHom_val_app_unit_tmul`: the morphism out of the
  tensor product sheaf determined by a bilinear pairing, evaluated on the sheafification-unit
  image of a pure tensor `a ⊗ₜ b`, is the value of the pairing on `a` and `b`.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.pairingApp_bilinearEquivTensorSheafHom_symm`: the bilinear pairing
  recovered from a morphism out of the tensor product sheaf pairs two local sections by sending
  the sheafification-unit image of their tensor through that morphism.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.unit_comp_bilinearEquivTensorSheafHom_val`: the same statement for the
  forward direction, read as one equality of morphisms of presheaves of modules rather than
  sectionwise.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.inverseImageBilinearEquiv_apply_coe_eq_unit_comp` and
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.inverseImageBilinearEquiv_symm_apply_coe_eq_comp_counit`: the pairing
  produced by the bijection of Tag 03D3 and the pairing produced by its inverse, written out
  with no `Equiv` left — the unit of `f⁻¹ ⊣ f_*` followed by the direct image of the pairing, and
  the inverse product comparison followed by the inverse image of the pairing followed by the
  counit.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.pairingApp_inverseImageBilinearEquiv`: the value of that pairing on a
  pair of local sections, which is the above transported through the sections functor.

## Implementation notes

Nothing here carries a `stacks` attribute: these are section-level computations of existing
comparison isomorphisms and the source states none of them.

A formula on *individual sections* is available for the universal property of the tensor product
sheaf because both sides of that bijection are described by sections: a bilinear pairing is a
map of sheaves of sets, read on sections by `Stacks.SheafOfModules.pairingApp`, and the tensor
product sheaf is the sheafification of a presheaf whose sections are spanned by pure tensors. It
is *not* available for `Stacks.SheafOfModules.inverseImageBilinearEquiv`. That bijection is the
transposition across the adjunction `f⁻¹ ⊣ f_*` carried by a
`CategoryTheory.Sheaf.MorphismOfTopoi`, and in that structure the two functors and the adjunction
are data with no description on sections — the direct image `f_*N` of a sheaf of modules has no
formula for its sections over an object, so neither does the transposed pairing. The best that can
be said is `Stacks.SheafOfModules.pairingApp_inverseImageBilinearEquiv`: the pair of sections is
carried through the unit of the adjunction and then through the direct image of the pairing. The
remaining content of step 3 of the chain of Tag 03EL is therefore the two morphism-level formulas,
and a statement of Tag 07A4 on pure tensors has to leave the topos unit and counit in place where
step 3 occurs.

`Stacks.SheafOfModules.pairingApp_inverseImageBilinearEquiv` is proved in term mode. Its two sides
spell the source of the pairing upstairs two ways —
`f.inverseImage.obj (moduleSheaf O F) ⨯ f.inverseImage.obj (moduleSheaf O G)` in the product
comparison and
`moduleSheaf _ ((inverseImageModules f O).obj F) ⨯ moduleSheaf _ ((inverseImageModules f O).obj G)`
in the pairing — and the two agree only at default transparency, so `rw` reports "did not find an
occurrence" of a pattern that is visibly present, with Lean's own note that the target is not
type-correct at the `implicit` level. For the same reason the two pure-tensor formulas evaluate a
composite of morphisms of presheaves of modules by `CategoryTheory.comp_apply` and
`CategoryTheory.congr_fun` rather than by rewriting with `PresheafOfModules.comp_app`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 03D3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03D3)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03EL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03EL)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05NA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05NA)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory Limits AlgebraicGeometry MonoidalCategory CategoryTheory.Sheaf
open AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules Stacks.Sheaves.RingedToposModules
open Stacks.Sheaves.ToposPullback Stacks.Sheaves.ToposPushforward
open Stacks.PresheafOfModules.ChangeOfRings

universe w v u

namespace Stacks.SheafOfModules

/-! ## The universal property of the tensor product sheaf on pure tensors -/

section TensorSheaf

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
  [J.HasSheafCompose (forget RingCat.{w})] [J.HasSheafCompose (forget AddCommGrpCat.{w})]
  [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}] [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
  {A : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ CommRingCat.{w}} {hA : Presheaf.IsSheaf J (ringPresheaf A)}
  {F G N : SheafOfModules.{w} (commRingSheaf J A hA)}

omit [J.HasSheafCompose (forget RingCat.{w})] [J.HasSheafCompose (forget AddCommGrpCat.{w})] in
/-- `Stacks.SheafOfModules.tensorSheafHomEquivPresheafTensorHom` is precomposition with the
sheafification unit: a morphism of sheaves of modules out of the tensor product sheaf restricts
along `F ⊗ G ⟶ (F ⊗ G)^#` to a morphism of presheaves of modules out of the objectwise tensor
product. This is the unit form of the hom-set bijection of the sheafification adjunction, and it
is the handle every formula below is read off from. -/
lemma tensorSheafHomEquivPresheafTensorHom_apply
    (t : ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, v, w, w, w}
      ⟨A, Presheaf.isSheaf_of_isSheaf_comp _ A (forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat) hA⟩).obj F).obj G ⟶
        N) :
    tensorSheafHomEquivPresheafTensorHom (hA := hA) t =
      (PresheafOfModules.sheafificationAdjunction (R := commRingSheaf J A hA) (𝟙 _)).unit.app
          (_root_.PresheafOfModules.tensorObj F.val G.val) ≫ t.val :=
  (PresheafOfModules.sheafificationAdjunction (R := commRingSheaf J A hA)
    (𝟙 _)).homEquiv_unit _ _ t

/-- **The morphism out of the tensor product sheaf determined by a bilinear pairing, read on the
objectwise tensor product.** Restricted along the sheafification unit it is the morphism out of
the objectwise tensor product determined by the same pairing. This is the whole content of
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.bilinearEquivTensorSheafHom` in the forward direction, as one equality of
morphisms of presheaves of modules; see
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.bilinearEquivTensorSheafHom_val_app_unit_tmul` for the sectionwise form. -/
lemma unit_comp_bilinearEquivTensorSheafHom_val
    (q : { q : moduleSheaf (commRingSheaf J A hA) F ⨯ moduleSheaf (commRingSheaf J A hA) G ⟶
        moduleSheaf (commRingSheaf J A hA) N //
      IsBilinearPairing (commRingSheaf J A hA) q }) :
    (PresheafOfModules.sheafificationAdjunction (R := commRingSheaf J A hA) (𝟙 _)).unit.app
          (_root_.PresheafOfModules.tensorObj F.val G.val) ≫
        (bilinearEquivTensorSheafHom (hA := hA) q).val =
      tensorHomOfPairing (hO := hA) q.2 :=
  (tensorSheafHomEquivPresheafTensorHom_apply (hA := hA) (bilinearEquivTensorSheafHom (hA := hA)
      q)).symm.trans
    (Equiv.apply_symm_apply (tensorSheafHomEquivPresheafTensorHom (hA := hA) (F := F) (G := G) (N :=
        N))
      (tensorHomOfPairing (hO := hA) q.2))

/-- Evaluating a composite of morphisms of presheaves of modules on a section. -/
private lemma app_apply_eq_of_comp_eq {R : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ RingCat.{w}}
    {X Y Z : _root_.PresheafOfModules.{w} R} {φ : X ⟶ Y} {ψ : Y ⟶ Z} {χ : X ⟶ Z}
    (h : φ ≫ ψ = χ) (U : Cᵒᵖ) (x : X.obj U) :
    ψ.app U (φ.app U x) = χ.app U x :=
  (CategoryTheory.comp_apply (PresheafOfModules.Hom.app φ U) (PresheafOfModules.Hom.app ψ U)
    x).symm.trans (CategoryTheory.congr_fun (congrArg (fun m ↦ PresheafOfModules.Hom.app m U) h) x)

/-- **The morphism out of the tensor product sheaf determined by a bilinear pairing, on a pure
tensor.** The sheafification unit carries a pure tensor `a ⊗ₜ b` of two local sections to a local
section of `F ⊗_A G`, and the morphism determined by the pairing `q` takes that section to the
value of `q` on `a` and `b`. This is the value formula for the direction of
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.bilinearEquivTensorSheafHom` which step 4 of the chain of Tag 03EL
traverses forwards and step 2 traverses backwards. -/
lemma bilinearEquivTensorSheafHom_val_app_unit_tmul
    (q : { q : moduleSheaf (commRingSheaf J A hA) F ⨯ moduleSheaf (commRingSheaf J A hA) G ⟶
        moduleSheaf (commRingSheaf J A hA) N //
      IsBilinearPairing (commRingSheaf J A hA) q }) (U : Cᵒᵖ)
    (a : F.val.obj U) (b : G.val.obj U) :
    (bilinearEquivTensorSheafHom (hA := hA) q).val.app U
        (((PresheafOfModules.sheafificationAdjunction (R := commRingSheaf J A hA) (𝟙 _)).unit.app
            (_root_.PresheafOfModules.tensorObj F.val G.val)).app U
          (a ⊗ₜ[(A ⋙ forget₂ CommRingCat.{w} RingCat.{w}).obj U] b)) =
      pairingApp (commRingSheaf J A hA) q.1 U a b :=
  (app_apply_eq_of_comp_eq
      (unit_comp_bilinearEquivTensorSheafHom_val (hA := hA) q) U _).trans
    (tensorHomOfPairing_app_tmul (hO := hA) q.2 U a b)

/-- **The bilinear pairing recovered from a morphism out of the tensor product sheaf, on a pair of
local sections.** It pairs `a` and `b` by sending the sheafification-unit image of `a ⊗ₜ b`
through the morphism. This is the value formula for the direction of
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.bilinearEquivTensorSheafHom` which step 2 of the chain of Tag 03EL
traverses forwards and step 4 traverses backwards. -/
lemma pairingApp_bilinearEquivTensorSheafHom_symm
    (t : ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, v, w, w, w}
      ⟨A, Presheaf.isSheaf_of_isSheaf_comp _ A (forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat) hA⟩).obj F).obj G ⟶
        N) (U : Cᵒᵖ)
    (a : F.val.obj U) (b : G.val.obj U) :
    pairingApp (commRingSheaf J A hA)
        ((bilinearEquivTensorSheafHom (hA := hA) (F := F) (G := G) (N := N)).symm t).1 U a b =
      t.val.app U
        (((PresheafOfModules.sheafificationAdjunction (R := commRingSheaf J A hA) (𝟙 _)).unit.app
            (_root_.PresheafOfModules.tensorObj F.val G.val)).app U
          (a ⊗ₜ[(A ⋙ forget₂ CommRingCat.{w} RingCat.{w}).obj U] b)) :=
  (pairingApp_pairingOfTensorHom (hO := hA)
      (tensorSheafHomEquivPresheafTensorHom (hA := hA) (F := F) (G := G) (N := N) t) U a b).trans
    (app_apply_eq_of_comp_eq
      (tensorSheafHomEquivPresheafTensorHom_apply (hA := hA) t).symm U _).symm

end TensorSheaf

/-! ## The inverse-image bijection, written out -/

section InverseImage

universe w' v' u'

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {D : Type u'} [Category.{v'} D]
  {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {K : GrothendieckTopology D}
  [J.HasSheafCompose (forget RingCat.{w})] [K.HasSheafCompose (forget RingCat.{w'})]
  [J.HasSheafCompose (forget AddCommGrpCat.{w})]
  [K.HasSheafCompose (forget AddCommGrpCat.{w'})]
  (f : MorphismOfTopoi (Sheaf J (Type w)) (Sheaf K (Type w')))
  (O : Sheaf K RingCat.{w'}) (F G : SheafOfModules.{w'} O)
  (N : SheafOfModules.{w} (inverseImageRingSheaf f O))

/-- The inverse of `Stacks.SheafOfModules.inverseImagePairingEquiv` transposes a pairing back
across the adjunction `f⁻¹ ⊣ f_*` and composes with the inverse of the product comparison. This
is the counterpart of `Stacks.SheafOfModules.inverseImagePairingEquiv_apply`. -/
lemma inverseImagePairingEquiv_symm_apply
    (p : moduleSheaf O F ⨯ moduleSheaf O G ⟶
      moduleSheaf O ((directImageModules f O).obj N)) :
    (inverseImagePairingEquiv f O F G N).symm p =
      (PreservesLimitPair.iso f.inverseImage (moduleSheaf O F) (moduleSheaf O G)).inv ≫
        (f.adj.homEquiv (moduleSheaf O F ⨯ moduleSheaf O G)
          (moduleSheaf (inverseImageRingSheaf f O) N)).symm p := rfl

/-- `Stacks.SheafOfModules.inverseImageBilinearEquiv` is
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.inverseImagePairingEquiv` on underlying pairings: the bilinearity of the
image is carried along, and is not part of the value. -/
lemma inverseImageBilinearEquiv_apply_coe
    (q : { q : moduleSheaf (inverseImageRingSheaf f O) ((inverseImageModules f O).obj F) ⨯
        moduleSheaf (inverseImageRingSheaf f O) ((inverseImageModules f O).obj G) ⟶
          moduleSheaf (inverseImageRingSheaf f O) N //
      IsBilinearPairing (inverseImageRingSheaf f O) q }) :
    (inverseImageBilinearEquiv f O F G N q).1 = inverseImagePairingEquiv f O F G N q.1 := rfl

/-- The inverse of `Stacks.SheafOfModules.inverseImageBilinearEquiv` is the inverse of
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.inverseImagePairingEquiv` on underlying pairings. -/
lemma inverseImageBilinearEquiv_symm_apply_coe
    (p : { p : moduleSheaf O F ⨯ moduleSheaf O G ⟶
        moduleSheaf O ((directImageModules f O).obj N) // IsBilinearPairing O p }) :
    ((inverseImageBilinearEquiv f O F G N).symm p).1 =
      (inverseImagePairingEquiv f O F G N).symm p.1 := rfl

/-- **The pairing into the direct image produced by the bijection of Tag 03D3.** It is the unit
of `f⁻¹ ⊣ f_*` followed by the direct image of the given pairing precomposed with the product
comparison of `f⁻¹`. This is the value formula for the direction of
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.inverseImageBilinearEquiv` which step 3 of the chain of Tag 03EL traverses
backwards. -/
lemma inverseImageBilinearEquiv_apply_coe_eq_unit_comp
    (q : { q : moduleSheaf (inverseImageRingSheaf f O) ((inverseImageModules f O).obj F) ⨯
        moduleSheaf (inverseImageRingSheaf f O) ((inverseImageModules f O).obj G) ⟶
          moduleSheaf (inverseImageRingSheaf f O) N //
      IsBilinearPairing (inverseImageRingSheaf f O) q }) :
    (inverseImageBilinearEquiv f O F G N q).1 =
      f.adj.unit.app (moduleSheaf O F ⨯ moduleSheaf O G) ≫
        f.pushforward.map
          (prodComparison f.inverseImage (moduleSheaf O F) (moduleSheaf O G) ≫ q.1) :=
  f.adj.homEquiv_unit _ _ _

/-- **The pairing of the inverse images produced by the inverse of the bijection of Tag 03D3.**
It is the inverse product comparison of `f⁻¹`, followed by the inverse image of the given
pairing, followed by the counit of `f⁻¹ ⊣ f_*`. This is the value formula for the direction of
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.inverseImageBilinearEquiv` which step 3 of the chain of Tag 03EL traverses
forwards. -/
lemma inverseImageBilinearEquiv_symm_apply_coe_eq_comp_counit
    (p : { p : moduleSheaf O F ⨯ moduleSheaf O G ⟶
        moduleSheaf O ((directImageModules f O).obj N) // IsBilinearPairing O p }) :
    ((inverseImageBilinearEquiv f O F G N).symm p).1 =
      (PreservesLimitPair.iso f.inverseImage (moduleSheaf O F) (moduleSheaf O G)).inv ≫
        f.inverseImage.map p.1 ≫
          f.adj.counit.app (moduleSheaf (inverseImageRingSheaf f O) N) :=
  congrArg (fun m ↦ (PreservesLimitPair.iso f.inverseImage (moduleSheaf O F)
    (moduleSheaf O G)).inv ≫ m) (f.adj.homEquiv_counit _ _ _)

/-- The value on a pair of local sections of the pairing into the direct image produced by the
bijection of Tag 03D3: carry the pair through the unit of `f⁻¹ ⊣ f_*`, then through the direct
image of the given pairing. The unit is where this stops: for a
`CategoryTheory.Sheaf.MorphismOfTopoi` the direct image has no description on sections, so neither
has the transposed pairing. -/
lemma pairingApp_inverseImageBilinearEquiv
    (q : { q : moduleSheaf (inverseImageRingSheaf f O) ((inverseImageModules f O).obj F) ⨯
        moduleSheaf (inverseImageRingSheaf f O) ((inverseImageModules f O).obj G) ⟶
          moduleSheaf (inverseImageRingSheaf f O) N //
      IsBilinearPairing (inverseImageRingSheaf f O) q }) (U : Dᵒᵖ)
    (a : (sectionsFunctor K U).obj (moduleSheaf O F))
    (b : (sectionsFunctor K U).obj (moduleSheaf O G)) :
    pairingApp O (inverseImageBilinearEquiv f O F G N q).1 U a b =
      (sectionsFunctor K U).map
          (f.pushforward.map
            (prodComparison f.inverseImage (moduleSheaf O F) (moduleSheaf O G) ≫ q.1))
        ((sectionsFunctor K U).map (f.adj.unit.app (moduleSheaf O F ⨯ moduleSheaf O G))
          (Functor.prodObjMk a b)) :=
  (congrArg (fun m ↦ (sectionsFunctor K U).map m (Functor.prodObjMk a b))
      (inverseImageBilinearEquiv_apply_coe_eq_unit_comp f O F G N q)).trans
    ((sectionsFunctor K U).map_comp_apply _ _ _)

end InverseImage

end Stacks.SheafOfModules

end
